<title>USA: Illinois Superconductor director resigns.</title>
<headline>Illinois Superconductor director resigns.</headline>
<dateline>MOUNT PROSPECT, Ill. 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Illinois Superconductor Corp said Wednesday Michael Friduss resigned from the board of directors, citing time commitments related to his growing consulting business.</p>
<p>The company said it has no immediate plans to replace Friduss.</p>
<p>Recently, a shareholder proposed the entire board, with the exception of chairman Ora Smith, resign. Sheldon Drobny, who according to a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission owns a 7.7 percent stake in the company, proposed other shareholders replace the current board, but the board rejected the proposal.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
